<Slide style={{ width: '1280px', height: '720px', background: '#FFFFFF', position: 'relative', fontFamily: 'Source Han Sans, Noto Sans CJK SC, sans-serif' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: '100%', height: 60, background: '#330662' }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', padding: '14px 60px' }}>What AI did, what was kept, what was rejected</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 100, left: 60, width: 1160, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 8 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>ACCOUNTABILITY IN A DEVELOPMENT LOG</Text>
    <Box style={{ width: 40, height: 3, background: '#57068C' }} />
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 160, left: 60, right: 60, height: 280, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'stretch', gap: 0 }}>
    {[
      { tag: 'STUDENT REQUEST', c: '#330662', t: '"Can you scaffold an obstacle spawner for the cart so the track is more dramatic?"', src: 'Student writes the request as a clear instruction, not a one-line prompt.' },
      { tag: 'AGENT RESPONSE', c: '#57068C', t: '"Here is a Unity script that places obstacles at intervals along the path. The cart has a forward velocity and respawns after collision."', src: 'The student copies a short summary of what the agent produced — enough to recall later, no more.' },
      { tag: 'STUDENT DECISION', c: '#7B5AA6', t: '"I replaced the spawner with a prebuilt track. The cart moves forward; the player only reacts. This feels more like being carried by the coaster than driving it."', src: 'This is where the emotional target meets the design choice. Without it, the AI’s output is just code.' },
    ].map((col, i, arr) => (
      <Box key={i} style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'stretch' }}>
        <Box style={{ flex: 1, padding: 18, background: col.c, borderRadius: i === 0 ? '10px 0 0 10px' : i === arr.length - 1 ? '0 10px 10px 0' : '0', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 10 }}>
          <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#FFC107', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>{col.tag}</Text>
          <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#FFFFFF', lineHeight: 1.5, fontStyle: 'italic' }}>{col.t}</Text>
          <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#EEE6F3', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>{col.src}</Text>
        </Box>
        {i < arr.length - 1 && (
          <Box style={{ width: 24, justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center', background: '#F6F1FA' }}>
            <Text style={{ fontSize: 24, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>→</Text>
          </Box>
        )}
      </Box>
    ))}
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 470, left: 60, right: 60, height: 170, padding: 22, background: '#F6F1FA', border: '1px solid #D9D0E4', borderRadius: 10, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 10 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold', letterSpacing: 2 }}>WHAT THE LOG MAKES POSSIBLE</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.55 }}>
      The log is not documentation. It is the trace that lets us answer the question the chat history cannot: <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>when the prototype diverged from the original emotional target, whose decision was it?</span>
    </Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>
      In The Darkroom, this trail runs 72 times. In Coaster Carnage, it runs 4 sessions plus a reflection. The trail is the artifact we study, not the build alone.
    </Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 680, left: 60, right: 60, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'space-between' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#8B97A8' }}>Xingchen Zhang · NYU Shanghai · XJTLU 2026 · Panel 11</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 14, color: '#57068C', fontWeight: 'bold' }}>10 / 16</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
